## Owner decision D9 — conversation_members self-enrollment gap (2026-10-07)

Discovered by the T4 performer and verified by the orchestrator on LOCAL: baseline policies on 
`public.conversation_members`
("Users can insert their own conversation preferences" WITH CHECK only user_id = caller; "Users can update their own
conversation preferences" with no WITH CHECK) plus INSERT/UPDATE grants to anon/authenticated let an authenticated user
add themselves to any conversation, or move their own row to another conversation, through the Data API. That defeats 
every
members-only rule (messages, attachments, receipts, mentions, roster, typing topic). App code does not need these 
client
writes: memberships come from the SECURITY DEFINER trigger `sync_conversation_members`, and the preferences/archive 
routes
write with the service-role client after `requireConversationParticipant`.
Asked (native question UI, pt-BR) whether to fix it in this phase. Owner chose: "Corrigir nesta fase (Recomendado)" — 
a new
task with a migration removing client creation/move of memberships, applied online with the others at T23, under the 
PLAN
and task review gates. To be planned as a replan (new task ID T28) after T4 closes.

