- Review rounds: a task's adversarial review that returns only Low findings (or approve with Lows) closes the gate; 
Lows are fixed or rejected and recorded in TRACK without a further review round. A High or Medium (including one the 
orchestrator rejects) still requires another round. Final whole-diff review (T22) unchanged.
- Regression cadence: per task, the Phase 4 regression E2E runs in Chrome only (`npx playwright test -c 
playwright.messaging-phase5.config.ts --project=regression-chrome`), plus the messaging DB suite when server code 
changes; the full Chrome + Edge regression runs at phase end (T22) and whenever a task touches the runner or shared 
fixtures. New specs still need 3 consecutive passing runs in Chrome and in Edge (AC-036, SPEC unchanged).
- Scope unchanged (no SPEC change); PLAN tasks, dependencies and acceptance unchanged, so no replan; the PLAN Standing 
rule "Regression" is annotated with D10.

