spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/TRACK.md:331:- Mechanisms: error = frame shaping (injected `phx_error`; 
later joins forwarded, real reply withheld, error `phx_reply` injected; no per-topic server error reachable on local 
Realtime v2.112.6); timeout = `phx_error` kick then join replies withheld so the SDK's own 10 s timer fires TIMED_OUT 
(sequence starts CHANNEL_ERROR; armed-before-join gives pure TIMED_OUT, not exercised); close = real server mechanism 
(one injected `access_token` push with an invalid token on the target topic → server `system` error + `phx_close`, 
only that channel ends; client CLOSED, no rejoin; later app joins withheld until `restore()`).
